/-!
# Exact entropy certificates for anchored windows: the type graph

`Z32/ModelEntropy.lean` measures the model system of the base `3/2` with
`φ_model(U)`, the growth rate of the carry language of the orbits confined to
`U`, and supplies its two extreme colours: block certificates giving
`φ_model = 0`, and horseshoes giving `φ_model > 0`.  This file fills the gap
between them for the **anchored windows** `U = [0, ℓ)` with `ℓ ≤ 1/2` — the
family Mahler's Z-numbers live at the top of (`ℓ = 1/2`, `Z32/FlattoCount.lean`)
— with two-sided enclosures sharp to eight decimals, and it does so with an
*exact* finite model, not an over-approximation.

## The type coordinate

For `ℓ ≤ 1/2` the carry of a confined model orbit is forced into `{0,1}`
(`TypeCert.carry_eq`), so the system is the greedy `3/2`-transformation
restricted to the window.  The cylinder of a carry word — the set of starting
points realising it — is an interval, and the *image* of that interval under the
composed map is an interval whose left endpoint is always `0`.  Hence a
cylinder's entire future is determined by a single rational number, the image's
right endpoint `t`; call it the cylinder's **type**.  Types transform by

`t --s--> min (ℓ, (3t − s)/2)`, kept exactly when the result is positive,

which is `TypeCert.child2` after clearing the common denominator `D`
(`t = a/D`, `ℓ = L/D`) and doubling, so that the whole transition is the
division-free integer identity `2 · child = min (2L) (3a − sD)`.

Two facts make this a *finite exact* model rather than an approximation.

* **Exactness.**  The length-`k` words of the type graph are exactly the
  length-`k` carry words of the window: `card_modelLang_eq`.  Soundness
  (`exists_state_path`) is the forward inclusion; realizability
  (`exists_orbit_of_mem_words`) is the reverse, and is where the certificate
  earns its lower bounds.  There is no over-counting to fight, so the *same*
  finite graph carries both bounds.
* **Finiteness.**  For every rational `ℓ < 1/2` the reachable type set is
  finite — measured over the whole grid of `§ Measurements`, sizes `3…936`.
  Only `ℓ = 1/2` itself is infinite (there the types are Flatto's aperiodic
  `f^k 1 / 2`), and that case is exactly what `Z32/FlattoCount.lean` computes by
  hand.

On top of the graph sit the vector certificates of
`ForMathlib/Combinatorics/PathGrowth.lean`: a weight `v` and rationals `a/b`,
`a'/b'` with `b·(Mv) ≤ a·v` and `a'·v ≤ b'·(Mv)` entrywise in `ℕ`, giving
`log(a'/b') ≤ φ_model([0,ℓ)) ≤ log(a/b)`.  The graph is deterministic (source
and label determine the target — a corollary of the transition identity, not a
separate check), which is what makes the lower bound available at all.

## Main results

* `TypeCert`, `TypeCert.ok` — the certificate and its integer-only validity
  check; `decide`-checkable, no `native_decide`, no floating point, no rational
  arithmetic in the kernel.
* `TypeCert.card_modelLang_eq` — the exact identity
  `Nat.card (modelLang 3 2 [0,ℓ) k) = #(words (type graph) k)`.
* `TypeCert.phiModel_le`, `TypeCert.le_phiModel` — the two enclosures.
* `phiModel_band_mem_Icc` — the flagship: `φ_model([0, 5/12))` to eight
  decimals, `0.32228460… ∈ [log 1.38027756, log 1.38027757]`.  This supersedes
  the ledger entry `Z32.log_fourteen_div_ten_le_phiModel_band`
  (`(log 14)/10 = 0.2639…`) and is the first *upper* bound on that window.
* `phiModel_top_band_mem_Icc` — the same at `ℓ = 23/48 = 0.47916…`, a
  three-state certificate small enough to check by hand.  Five further windows
  are certified in `§ The entries`, giving a seven-row atlas across
  `[0.4, 0.48]`.

